            <ArticleTitle>Liver accessory lobe torsion in the infant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>153-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of vomiting and selective epigastric pain secondary to volvulus of the pedicle of a liver accessory lobe, in an infant, is reported. Ultrasonic findings are useful and probably sufficient for a correct diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
